        "heading": "The skin microbiome",
        "standfirst": "<p>The bacteria living on your skin are part of how healthy skin works. Here is what the research shows, and where it stops.</p>",
        "intro": "<p>Most of us grow up thinking of bacteria as something to get rid of. Your skin is home to a busy community of bacteria, fungi and other microbes, known as the skin microbiome, and the research suggests they help skin defend itself and keep its barrier working. As one review put it, with the microbiome you are never alone.</p>",
